   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Relevant CPD 2021-2025 Output Indicator: 4.3.3. Number of technology solutions used for management of harmful chemicals</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicators
1st Relevant CPD 2021-2025 Output Indicator:
4.3.3. Number of technology solutions used for management of harmful chemicals
Project Output Indicator 1: Adoption/implementation of ODS legislation and regulation to control and monitor ODS consumption 
Project Output Indicator 2: 
Efficient and timely data collection and reporting
Project Output Indicator 3: Consultations and coordination with other national gencies/stakeholders
Project Output Indicator 4: 
Supervision of timely implementation of phase-out activities and reduction in ODS consumption
Project Output Indicator 5:
Awareness and Publication
Project Output Indicator 6:
Regional cooperation and participation in Montreal Protocol meetings

Data validates that Indicative CP output indicators is partially achieved and expected to be fully achieved by the end of the CPD (2020), through project intervention.
The project supported the Directorate of Climate Change Mitigation in the development of the REKOMBPO application and MontiR-AC application. Those applications are used for the mitigation of ODS for importers and HFCs in the domestic sector.
Data validates that output indicators is partially achieved and expected to be fully achieved by the end of the year.
1.a Facilitating technical meetings related to data mechanism delivery between SNANK (Sistem Nasional Neraca Komoditas) and the REKOMBPO application on February 9, 2023, and May 31, 2023.  
1.b Facilitating a meeting related to the formulation of an Urgency/Explanation Paper for Implementation Regulations as the Implementation of the Montreal Protocol on February 17, 2023. 

1.c Supporting Indonesian Delegate for Kigali Implementation Plan (KIP) Preparation Workshop on February 27, 2023. 
1.d Facilitating a meeting related to the Implementation of Montreal Protocol Regulations on March 6, 2023. 
1.e Facilitating a series of meetings related to formulation Ministerial Regulation concerning Procedures of ODS and HFC Recommendations on April 5, 2023; April 13, 2023; May 19, 2023; May 24-25, 2023; June 14, 2023, and June 20, 2023.
1.f Facilitating a meeting related to changes in Guidelines and Technical Guidelines of Operational Assistance to the System House
Data validates that output indicators is partially achieved and expected to be fully achieved by the end of the year.
2.a Facilitating a meeting for the preparation of ODS and HFC Consumption Reports to the Multilateral Fund and Ozone Secretariate on April 17-18, 2023. 
2.b Convening a HFC Mapping Kick-Off Meeting on May 23, 2023.  
2.c Facilitating a meeting related to the HFC Report for the year 2020-2021 on June 9, 2023.

Data validates that output indicators is partially achieved and expected to be fully achieved by the end of the year.
Facilitating a meeting related to formulation Explanation Paper for the preparation of the draft of Presidential Regulation on National Policy and Strategy for ODS and HFC regulation on February 10, 2023.
Data validates that output indicators is partially achieved and expected to be fully achieved by the end of the year.
The project will conduct supervision related to ODS and HFC consumption in the second semester of 2023.
Data validates that output indicators is partially achieved and expected to be fully achieved by the end of the year.
Convening a socialization meeting on the Presidential Regulation Number 129 of 2022 concerning The Ratification of the Amendment to the Montreal Protocol on Substances that Deplete the Ozone Layer, Kigali, 2016 on January 25, 2023. This activity successfully covered by 19 media coverage accros Indonesia, and 1 (one) press release published by Bureau of Public Relations Ministry of Environment and Forestry.
Data validates that output indicators is partially achieved and expected to be fully achieved by the end of the year.
Supporting Indonesian Delegate for the forty-fifth meeting of the Open-ended Working Group (OEWG45) of the Parties to the Montreal Protocol on Substances that Deplete</narrative>
